VALUES (460009382302012, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Evaporation. Introduction to Recycle & By-pass operation. in the context of “Material Balance In Process Without Chemical Reactions”. Define it, state its key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Simple M.B. problems on operations like Drying in the context of “Material Balance In Process Without Chemical Reactions”. Define it, state its key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain power in the context of “Introduction”. Define it, state its key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Ideal Gas Law. NTP & STP in the context of “Basic Chemical Calculations”. Define it, state its key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Evaporation removes solvent as vapor to concentrate a solution; heat supply, boiling point elevation and product sensitivity matter.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Material Balance In Process Without Chemical Reactions; Definition of Law of Conversation of Mass; Process flow diagram; significance of Material balance in chemical industry. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Material Balance In Process Without Chemical Reactions. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with offici