stent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Introduction. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** The ideal gas equation PV=nRT relates pressure, volume, moles and absolute temperature under ideal-gas assumptions.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Basic Chemical Calculations; Definition of Atomic weight and Molecular wt.; Calculation of Molecular weight of various compounds; Introduction to Avogadro’s Number & Moles concept. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Basic Chemical Calculations. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with official teaching material."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

