re applicable and state one way to verify the result and a relevant limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Introduction; Dimensions and systems of units; Fundamental quantities; Derived quantities. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Introduction. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Introduction to Avogadro’s Number & Moles concept is listed under “Basic Chemical Calculations” in the course syllabus. Define the concept, explain the main process steps or governing conditions, relate it to Basic Chemical Calculations, Definition of Atomic weight and Molecular wt., Calculation of Molecular weight of various compounds, relation between Mole and Atomic weight, and apply it to a chemical-engineering example. Use consistent quantities/units where applicable and state one way to verify the result and a relevant limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Basic Chemical Calculations; Definition of Atomic weight and Molecular wt.; Calculation of Molecular weight of various compounds; relation between Mole and Atomic weight. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Basic Chemical Calculations. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with official teaching material."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

