INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (4600913103020125, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Basic permutation in the context of Permutation and Combination. Define it, describe its key principles or steps, and give one example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Classical probability in the context of Probability. Define it, describe its key principles or steps, and give one example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Binomial theorem (without proof) for positive integral index (expansion and general form in the context of Binomial Theorem. Define it, describe its key principles or steps, and give one example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Definition in the context of Differentiation. Define it, describe its key principles or steps, and give one example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** A permutation counts arrangements in which order matters; arranging r distinct objects selected from n gives n!/(n−r)!.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to syllabus points such as Basic combination; Permutation and Combination. State relevant rules, components or assumptions and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Mathematics-III task. Identify the objective, explain the selected procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention an important limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** For equally likely outcomes, classical probability is favourable outcomes divided by all outcomes. The complement rule is P(not A)=1−P(A).\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to syllabus points such as Compliment of event; Probability. State relevant rules, components or assumptions and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Mathematics-III task. Identify the objective, explain the selected procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention an important limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** The binomial theorem expands a power of a sum using binomial coefficients and the exponents of the terms.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to syllabus points such as Binomial theorem for any index (expansion without proof) first and second binomial approximation with applications to engineering problems; Binomial Theorem. State relevant rules, components or assumptions and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Mathematics-III task. Identify the objective, explain the selected procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention an important limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Definition is covered in the syllabus unit “Differentiation”. A complete answer should define the concept, describe its role and steps/components, relate it to Some properties, Derivative of some important functions, Chain rule, Derivative of implicit function, provide a practical example, and state a relevant check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and connect it to syllabus points such as Some properties; Derivative of some important functions; Chain rule; Derivative of implicit function. State relevant rules, components or assumptions and how they affect the outcome.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a concrete Mathematics-III task. Identify the objective, explain the selected procedure, and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective; mention an important limitation, error source or trade-off. Conclude why the approach fits the task.\n\nMarking guide: definition/purpose 2; principles/steps 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

