VALUES (460009382303011, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain Hazard Identification and control Techaniques in the context of “Hazard Identification and control Techaniques”. Define it, state its key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain Classification of Chemical Hazards in the context of “Hazard Identification and control Techaniques”. Define it, state its key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain respiratory organs in the context of “Safety, Safety codes and standards, PPE”. Define it, state its key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain occupational health hazards and control in the context of “Hazard Identification and control Techaniques”. Define it, state its key principles or steps, and give one relevant example."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Hazard Identification and control Techaniques is listed under “Hazard Identification and control Techaniques” in the course syllabus. Define the concept, explain the main process steps or governing conditions, relate it to Deffination of Hazards and types Hazards, Classification of Chemical Hazards, occupational health hazards and control, Prevention of diseases due to chemical effect, and apply it to a chemical-engineering example. Use consistent quantities/units where applicable and state one way to verify the result and a relevant limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Deffination of Hazards and types Hazards; Classification of Chemical Hazards; occupational health hazards and control; Prevention of diseases due to chemical effect. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Hazard Identification and control Techaniques. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Classification of Chemical Hazards is listed under “Hazard Identification and control Techaniques” in the course syllabus. Define the concept, explain the main process steps or governing conditions, relate it to Hazard Identification and control Techaniques, Deffination of Hazards and types Hazards, occupational health hazards and control, Prevention of diseases due to chemical effect, and apply it to a chemical-engineering example. Use consistent quantities/units where applicable and state one way to verify the result and a relevant limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Hazard Identification and control Techaniques; Deffination of Hazards and types Hazards; occupational health hazards and control; Prevention of diseases due to chemical effect. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Hazard Identification and control Techaniques. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details w