VALUES (4600093823030110, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Analyze a process or equipment problem involving Chemical burns and their effect within “Control of Chemical Hazards”. Explain the principles, justify the selected method, and state a check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a process or equipment problem involving eyes within “Safety, Safety codes and standards, PPE”. Explain the principles, justify the selected method, and state a check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a process or equipment problem involving hands within “Safety, Safety codes and standards, PPE”. Explain the principles, justify the selected method, and state a check and one limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Analyze a process or equipment problem involving occupational health hazards and control within “Hazard Identification and control Techaniques”. Explain the principles, justify the selected method, and state a check and one limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Chemical burns and their effect is listed under “Control of Chemical Hazards” in the course syllabus. Define the concept, explain the main process steps or governing conditions, relate it to Control of Chemical Hazards, Ventilation and lighting, Safety factors: Heat and Temperature hazards, Thermal Hazards, and apply it to a chemical-engineering example. Use consistent quantities/units where applicable and state one way to verify the result and a relevant limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Control of Chemical Hazards; Ventilation and lighting; Safety factors: Heat and Temperature hazards; Thermal Hazards. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Control of Chemical Hazards. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** COD estimates chemically oxidizable matter in a water sample and is not identical to BOD.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Safety, Safety codes and standards, PPE; Definition of Safety; Importance of Safety in Chemical Industries; Development of safety organization. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Safety, Safety codes and standards, PPE. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** COD estimates chemically oxidizable matter in a water sample and is not identical to BOD.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Safety, Safety codes and standards, PPE; Definition of Safety; Importance of Safety in Chemical Industries; Development of safety organization. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Safety, Safety codes and standards, PPE. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with official teaching material."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** occupational health hazards and control is listed under “Hazard Identification and control Techaniques” in the course syllabus. Define the concept, explain the main process steps or governing conditions, relate it to Hazard Identification and control Techaniques, Deffination of Hazards and types Hazards, Classification of Chemical Hazards, Prevention of diseases due to chemical effect, and apply it to a chemical-engineering example. Use consistent quantities/units where applicable and state one way to verify the result and a relevant limitation.\n\n**Principles/procedure (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical sequence and relate it to Hazard Identification and control Techaniques; Deffination of Hazards and types Hazards; Classification of Chemical Hazards; Prevention of diseases due to chemical effect. Include the relevant process steps, equipment, variables or formulas. State assumptions and use consistent units where calculations are involved.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a process, equipment, laboratory or design question from Hazard Identification and control Techaniques. State the expected result and why the approach fits.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Compare the result with the stated process/design objective; note a relevant error source, safety consideration or limitation.\n\nMarking guide: meaning/purpose 2; principles/procedure 3; application/example 2; verification/conclusion 1. Confirm details with official teaching material."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

