VALUES (4600093823030135, ARRAY['"[8 marks] Explain and apply Definition of Safety in “Safety, Safety codes and standards, PPE”; include the main principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain and apply Ventilation and lighting in “Control of Chemical Hazards”; include the main principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain and apply Classification of Air Pollutants in “Air Pollution”; include the main principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] Explain and apply Introduction of Water Pollution in “Water Pollution & Waste Water Treatment”; include the main principle, an example and a verification or limitation."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Definition of Safety is covered in “Safety, Safety codes and standards, PPE”. Define its role, describe the main steps/components, connect it to Importance of Safety in Chemical Industries, Development of safety organization, Indian standards (IS) and codes, International Standards like ISO 9001, give a practical example, and add a verification check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Describe the concept in sequence and connect it with Importance of Safety in Chemical Industries, Development of safety organization, Indian standards (IS) and codes, International Standards like ISO 9001.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply the concept to a practical SAFETY & POLLUTION MEASURES task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and mention one limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Ventilation and lighting is covered in “Control of Chemical Hazards”. Define its role, describe the main steps/components, connect it to Safety factors: Heat and Temperature hazards, Thermal Hazards, Chemical burns and their effect, Colour codes and symbols for safety, give a practical example, and add a verification check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Describe the concept in sequence and connect it with Safety factors: Heat and Temperature hazards, Thermal Hazards, Chemical burns and their effect, Colour codes and symbols for safety.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply the concept to a practical SAFETY & POLLUTION MEASURES task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and mention one limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Classification of Air Pollutants is covered in “Air Pollution”. Define its role, describe the main steps/components, connect it to Sources of Air Pollution Effect of Air pollution on human health, animals and material Ambient air sampling, particulate and gaseous sample collection methods, give a practical example, and add a verification check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Describe the concept in sequence and connect it with Sources of Air Pollution Effect of Air pollution on human health, animals and material Ambient air sampling, particulate and gaseous sample collection methods.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply the concept to a practical SAFETY & POLLUTION MEASURES task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and mention one limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning (2):** Introduction of Water Pollution is covered in “Water Pollution & Waste Water Treatment”. Define its role, describe the main steps/components, connect it to Classification & Sources of Water Pollution Characterization of water : BOD, COD, Suspended Matter, Dissolved solids, give a practical example, and add a verification check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3):** Describe the concept in sequence and connect it with Classification & Sources of Water Pollution Characterization of water : BOD, COD, Suspended Matter, Dissolved solids.\n\n**Application/example (2):** Apply the concept to a practical SAFETY & POLLUTION MEASURES task and state the expected result.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1):** Check the result and mention one limitation or risk.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

